  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fostering Preparedness Actions for Response and Early Recovery to Increase Resilience to Multiple Risks of Urban and Peri-Urban Communities in the Regions of Amazonas and San Martin in Peru.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The convergence of unique meteorological, physical, ecological, and demographic factors makes Peru one of the most vulnerable countries to multi-hazards risks in the world. Despite the country&#x2019;s upper middle-income status, the geographical disparity in access and quality of basic public services deprives households of opportunities to improve their livelihoods and exacerbates vulnerabilities in case of emergencies. In the Amazonas and San Martin regions, greater exposition and occurrence of natural hazards overlapped with human-induced ones is combined with limited institutional and community-based preparedness and response capabilities. To increase resilience to multiple risks of urban and peri-urban communities in the regions of Amazonas and San Martin in Peru, this action is promoting: i) Communities in urban and peri-urban areas are better prepared to respond to emergencies and disasters and early recovery of livelihoods with an emphasis on better access to shock-responsive social protection</narrative>
  </description>
